SrvPalette: publish the current colour pixel set instead of appending it

_DtCacheProperties() holds the "SDT Pixel Set" property that Motif's XmColorObj
reads to colour every CDE application: DtInitialize fetches it through the
colour server's selection, and the pixel sets in it are what CDE applications
paint their widgets with (the desktop colour comes from RESOURCE_MANAGER, but
applications do not take their widget colours from there).

It appended (PropModeAppend) a fresh copy on every palette change, so the
property accumulated every palette the session had ever used and grew without
bound.  A client then received whichever block the relay happened to hand it,
which Motif could not use, and the application fell back to its default colours.
Replace the property instead, and stop incrementing the cached string's length
on every call.  The value ends with the version byte, which is where Motif
expects it.
--- a/programs/dtsession/SrvPalette.c
+++ b/programs/dtsession/SrvPalette.c
@@ -345,12 +345,20 @@
        palette->converted_len = strlen(palette->converted);
      }
   
-  *(palette->converted + palette->converted_len) = XmPIXEL_SET_PROP_VERSION ;
-  palette->converted_len++ ;
-  palette->converted[palette->converted_len] = 0 ;
-  XChangeProperty(dpy, win, pixel_set_atom, XA_STRING, 8, PropModeAppend, 
-		 (unsigned char *) XtNewString(palette->converted), 
-		 palette->converted_len) ;
+  /*
+   * cde-wayland: publish the current pixel set, replacing whatever was there.
+   * Motif's XmColorObj reads this property to colour every CDE application, and
+   * it expects the value to be the set followed by the version byte.  Appending
+   * (PropModeAppend) instead left every palette the session had ever used in the
+   * property, growing it without bound, and a client could end up with a block
+   * it could not use -- leaving the application at Motif's default colours.
+   * The cached string's length is its own: the version byte overwrites its
+   * terminator, which is where Motif expects to find it.
+   */
+  palette->converted[palette->converted_len] = XmPIXEL_SET_PROP_VERSION ;
+  XChangeProperty(dpy, win, pixel_set_atom, XA_STRING, 8, PropModeReplace,
+		 (unsigned char *) palette->converted,
+		 palette->converted_len + 1) ;
 }
 
